  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_23fd713c147c4f908176b81ec06dd607",
      "statement": "An action requires two independent registrations: an implementation in internal/actions/<name>.go self-registered via init()+RegisterActionFactory, and a matching ActionDefinition in internal/catalog/catalog.go; neither is cross-checked against the other.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adding-a-trusted-action.md#L24-L39",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:485575966450eb60b731877675813ff59fab4dabdc2928fe5fcbc095f79a4687:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/actions/get_pull_secret_email.go#L16-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f4a2755995806b01679959b4fed4a821a0632e224080307aa53ac2f95a3ecead:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2fde1ac8577143478cf6629f90b1d48c",
      "statement": "If a catalog entry exists with no matching internal/actions implementation, the API accepts POST /{action}/run (202) but the worker fails the execution asynchronously with 'unknown action' when it calls actions.CreateAction.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adding-a-trusted-action.md#L34-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e0f576df92306d2048dcbe18674df864c4295371b50b3e9a1de8e9e4da42ff83:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_efcb940f32844f998f960c0ef7ab44bd",
      "statement": "If an internal/actions implementation exists with no matching catalog entry, GET /{action} and POST /{action}/run return 404 Unknown action because handlers validate the action name against the catalog before execution.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adding-a-trusted-action.md#L37-L39",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f543aa6473a70b9e775db3e4c10d777a2739c18df0a9af74e0db370564451bc5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9dd499736e5b4d69b6060ebc6b9db4a2",
      "statement": "A KubeAction implements RequiredRBAC(target) and UsesPodExec(); the executor builds a backplane client scoped to exactly those RBAC rules and only provisions a pod executor when UsesPodExec() returns true, so the action never constructs its own cluster credentials.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adding-a-trusted-action.md#L51-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1b4c276dbe8d1305e9283cd5456f4a4403b2bad33d1f829a6c0227045cc9fe52:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/actions/get_pull_secret_email.go#L37-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:39073f92f048a1b4b8a7cd5dd186883c0453e440e0ee3f72df927589f1480ba6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5da4f4c293dd4806a300a80fabd286b5",
      "statement": "An AWSAction implements RequiredServices(target) instead of RBAC rules and has no pod-exec path; a mutating AWS action must additionally implement AWSWriteAction (Operation(), Resource()).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adding-a-trusted-action.md#L76-L107",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e4e5cae817830e925f8a3c3e138a1807fb3863e1ef888506820ca9fa10e3b48d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/actions/aws_write.go#L96-L111",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a265b5e737bbbf52582d034ba08a9b8dbc0d3bb203b88bca10e0d6f051f6e6f3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0bde8d8b4874422bb08a34450a7a91b6",
      "statement": "AWSScope decides whether to treat an AWS action as a write purely via a type assertion to AWSWriteAction (internal/executor/aws.go); an action that mutates AWS state but implements only AWSAction is judged a read and runs without being checked against the ROSA_TA_AWS_ALLOWED_OPERATIONS write allowlist, regardless of the catalog's Type field.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adding-a-trusted-action.md#L95-L106",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5a309a2cbfcd20f721b66bce3386c8b367015aeaca8475f542ca2b974eb7d6eb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_43273ad615d2450e85ba6414cccc20f1",
      "statement": "AWSWriteAction's Operation() names the mutation and must appear in the operation allowlist to be authorized, and Resource() fixes the kind of object acted on so a caller-supplied resource parameter cannot redirect the write; aws_write.go additionally verifies cluster ownership tags on the target instance before mutating it, as a check layered on top of the AWSWriteAction gate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/actions/aws_write.go#L101-L140",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:390729120bdaf2337e8e089f3bf4423cac751a7fc0d84bef0c6b910df202c5d7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/actions/aws_write.go#L37-L94",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a98a7a2e9b975e2a1f6dd42e30eebc3eecc7d9204af6fa5530b0f5d399ad072d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4537e85834744074a03e7b31b624e055",
      "statement": "RegisterActionFactory takes a factory function rather than an instance so each execution gets a fresh action value, and the registry key returned by Name() must match the catalog Name exactly.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adding-a-trusted-action.md#L109-L120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2aa803dd7adea8d4947ca0f07e2be96c201aa1eae4efa07a52dbc1a41b4d5256:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/actions/get_pull_secret_email.go#L16-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f4a2755995806b01679959b4fed4a821a0632e224080307aa53ac2f95a3ecead:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cac2bc40408d4897970abd1d7ccc5f50",
      "statement": "The catalog's Required flag on a Params entry is descriptive only: the API does not reject a request for omitting a required parameter, returning 202 regardless, and a missing parameter only fails asynchronously once Execute runs, so the action itself must validate parameters at the boundary.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adding-a-trusted-action.md#L201-L207",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ade272389c12c6bb7f04af5fc87126dac75f8f0adf499ab55fdbf963ce7aa9de:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_28422929e3324d0ab5815739c05654cb",
      "statement": "Authorization enforces a namespace allowlist (ROSA_TA_ALLOWED_NAMESPACES) and a secret allowlist (ROSA_TA_ALLOWED_SECRETS) before an action executes; the secret allowlist check validates the caller-supplied target rather than what RequiredRBAC actually grants, and both checks are skipped in permissive mode when no namespace allowlist is configured.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adding-a-trusted-action.md#L213-L231",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:30d4c7cad790c6e988629bfdfb4897051c69e358ca47f28741b3b6f277a3c7f4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_197c7d2269f2494dba2a94d0334ff7b7",
      "statement": "cmd/action-cli wires up the full executor pipeline (authorization, audit, backplane/AWS client construction, execution) outside the server, dispatching on whether the action implements KubeAction or AWSAction, and resolves actions.CreateAction(action) by name exactly as the production worker does, so a missing init() registration fails identically in the CLI.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://cmd/action-cli/main.go#L107-L139",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cf9f361fd6856551dd5e44768a899cdc3b755385e57c0bd441e8b07b11a68339:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://cmd/action-cli/main.go#L76-L80",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:58c4a252aadb4ac36cc344ada4e14a8a160a59fb2c6f2c49f4d8cc75b42394ac:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8cca6a3f6ac24f33b1beb8848f3af991",
      "statement": "cmd/action-cli reads the same ROSA_TA_AWS_ALLOWED_REGIONS and ROSA_TA_AWS_ALLOWED_OPERATIONS environment variables the server reads, with no CLI-only override, so what it can exercise locally never exceeds what the server would permit in production.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://cmd/action-cli/main.go#L113-L139",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b5f18b00f4adc5304151c301f69f3ab68961e5469258d3a0b4b0fb30cd8b645d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4d202bb5609e45c3a093235071719ceb",
      "statement": "A local kubeconfig-backed KubeconfigProvider used for local/e2e testing ignores RequiredRBAC entirely, so neither cmd/action-cli nor a local kind-cluster run verifies RBAC correctness; that relies on unit tests and code review instead.",
